    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d48">

                <pb facs="0084" n="70" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg70"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC Indonesia/1–948: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in the Netherlands
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-01-09T18:00:00-05:00">January 9, 1948—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. For your info and possible future use if instructed, Dept officials made
                    strong informal representations Jan 8 to Helb, Counselor Neth Emb, to end that
                    his Govt would (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) promptly consider and accept
                    political principles set forth Graham’s 84<anchor n="1" xml:id="d48-f1"/>
                    (repeated Hague in Deptel 9, Jan 9) and (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)
                    indicate promptly to Van Zeeland its approval in <pb facs="0085" n="71"
                        xml:id="pg71"/> order Van Zeeland throw weight his support to proposals
                    within GOC. Dept informed personally and confidentially by Helb Jan 9 that
                    strong recommendation to FonOff to above effect has been made by Neth Emb.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
